# Test-only environment for `npm run test:integration` in the scraper
# workspace (T-279). Copy this file to `.env.test` (gitignored -- see the
# repo root .gitignore).
#
# NEVER copy the values from `scraper/.env` into this file. That file is the
# LIVE runtime env -- its DATABASE_HOST/DATABASE_URL point at the production
# Postgres host (103.118.16.189). Running integration tests against those
# values writes real insert/delete/upsert rows into prod (GitHub #163).
#
# If this file (or a `.env.test` copy of it) is missing, no DB/Redis env
# vars resolve and the global integration-test guard
# (tests/helpers/db-safety-guard.ts, wired via vitest.integration.setup.ts)
# refuses to run any test -- fail closed, not fail open.
#
# THE ONLY SANCTIONED TARGET (owner rule 2026-08-28: "Don't create any new
# database" -- there is no throwaway/local Postgres for this project, and
# none should ever be created). Full recipe, rebuild steps, and the "why
# does this file keep going missing" note:
# docs/ops/prod-ops-recipes.md - section 12 "Integration tests: the only
# sanctioned target" (issue #690).
#
# Database: `ipodhan_test`, on the one Windows-VPS Postgres instance
# (103.118.16.189), reached ONLY through the tunnel on localhost:15432
# (see docs/ops/prod-ops-recipes.md section 1). A second, undocumented
# tunnel may exist on port 5432 on this machine -- 5432 must NOT be used
# for tests; do not investigate or touch that process.
# Role: `ipodhan_app` (schemas moved to it 2026-09-09 so this database can
# be rebuilt unattended by a non-superuser -- see the rebuild recipe in
# section 12).
#
# The password is read BY NAME from D:\Abhay\GLOBAL.env at use-time --
# NEVER paste the value into this file or any other repo file:
#   PW=$(grep "^IPODHAN_APP_DB_PASSWORD=" D:/Abhay/GLOBAL.env | cut -d= -f2- | tr -d '"')

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://ipodhan_app:${PW}@localhost:15432/ipodhan_test
DATABASE_HOST=localhost
DATABASE_PORT=15432
DATABASE_NAME=ipodhan_test
DATABASE_USER=ipodhan_app
DATABASE_PASSWORD=${PW}

# Redis - an UNAUTHENTICATED local/CI Redis instance. Prod/staging Redis for
# this project always requires a password; the guard treats any
# password/auth as a prod-shaped signal and refuses to run. There is no
# sanctioned shared test Redis -- Postgres is the resource the "no new
# databases" rule covers; run Redis locally (`redis-server` or a disposable
# container) if a suite needs one.
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
REDIS_HOST=localhost
REDIS_PASSWORD=
